# 
# https://w3id.org/bmp#LightWeightConcrete

:LightWeightConcrete a owl:Class ;
	rdfs:subClassOf :Concrete ;
	rdfs:comment """Material Category: Concrete
What it is made of / How it's made: It is made by mixing cement, water, sand, and porous aggregates (like expanded clay or pumice). Alternatively, it can be made by injecting stable foam directly into a standard cement slurry to fill the structure with tiny bubbles.
Description: A structural or insulating concrete formulated with air-filled aggregates to drastically reduce its total weight (LightWeightConcrete).""" , "https://www.iso.org/standard/41260.html"@en ;
	rdfs:label "LightWeightConcrete"@en .
