# 
# https://w3id.org/bmp#WoodHard

:WoodHard a owl:Class ;
	rdfs:subClassOf :WoodTimber ;
	rdfs:comment """Material Category: Wood / Timber
What it is made of / How it's made: It is made of complex cellulose fibers derived from angiosperm trees (broad-leaved deciduous trees like Oak, Beech, Maple, and Ash). These trees grow very slowly, resulting in highly packed, tight growth rings with a dense, heavy microscopic pore structure.
Description: High-density, tough timber harvested from slow-growing, broad-leaved deciduous trees (WoodHard).""" , "https://www.iso.org/standard/77077.html"@en ;
	rdfs:label "WoodHard"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/bmp#WoodSoft

:WoodSoft a owl:Class ;
	rdfs:subClassOf :WoodTimber ;
	rdfs:comment """Material Category: Wood / Timber
What it is made of / How it's made: It is made of simpler cellulose structures derived from gymnosperm trees (needle-bearing evergreen conifers like Pine, Spruce, Fir, and Cedar). These trees grow rapidly, resulting in wider growth rings and a lighter, more flexible wood matrix.
Description: Lightweight, flexible timber harvested from fast-growing, needle-bearing coniferous evergreen trees (WoodSoft).""" , "https://www.iso.org/standard/77077.html"@en ;
	rdfs:label "WoodSoft"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/bmp#WoodTimber

:WoodTimber a owl:Class ;
	rdfs:comment "The wood and timber category includes organic, structural materials harvested from trees, consisting of complex cellulose fibers bound together by a natural glue called lignin. This category covers seasoned lumber dried naturally by open-air circulation (airdrytimber), flexible and fast-growing wood from cone-bearing evergreen trees (woodsoft), and dense, slow-growing wood from broad-leaved deciduous trees (woodhard)." , "https://www.iso.org/standard/77077.html"@en ;
	rdfs:label "Timber"@en , "Wood"@en .
